  "notes": [
    "The tenth and last Upgraded event the proxy emitted before the exploit, log 343 of block 19391308, selected implementation 0xa051fc7d38baa0ace811ad9de4e9f7024e5d8a30; the EIP-1967 implementation slot holds that address at block 19392760 and the artifact runtime code hash is identical at its deployment block 19390499 and at block 19392760. The exploited selector 0x1ef29a02 is present in this artifact and absent from the preceding implementation 0xf92ecf887a30d9afde76f5c220cc6dead59df540, so this upgrade is the change that made the defect-bearing code active.",
    "The 207 successful drain transactions between blocks 19392761 and 19394695, when Unizen rolled the proxy back to implementation 0xf92ecf887a30d9afde76f5c220cc6dead59df540, pull 245 approval balances from 191 distinct victim addresses across 57 ERC-20s and forward them to 31 receiver addresses. Each component is the exact sum of the Transfer events in which a victim address that receives nothing back in the transaction sends a token to the aggregator proxy and the same token leaves the proxy to a different address in the same transaction. USDT, USDC and DAI use par; every other component uses the DefiLlama observation nearest the incident timestamp, all of which lie between 2 seconds before and 105 seconds after it. Nine further drained tokens (0x102dc1840f0c3c179670f21fa63597e82df34e60, 0x6a7eff1e2c355ad6eb91bebb5ded49257f3fed98, 0x1bb9b64927e0c5e207c9db4093b3738eef5d8447, 0x12c51b8f1b8a98c70fe6ae45c158a78931423e4c, 0xe4b4c008ff36e3c50c4299c223504a480de9c833, 0x0f7b3f5a8fed821c5eb60049538a548db2d479ce, 0x1294f4183763743c7c9519bec51773fb3acd78fd, 0x1c001d1c9e8c7b8dc717c714d30b31480ab360f5, 0xe59b14e43479dc30d77f553e4b5c6fc67e1f6caf) have no DefiLlama observation and are excluded, so the total is a floor. Only the Ethereum aggregator is measured; Unizen’s onchain recovery notice also named Polygon and Avalanche return addresses, and those chains are not covered here. Reported figures of roughly 2.0-2.1 million USD track the single largest drain, the 2,176,228.712449 USDT taken in the anchor transaction and immediately swapped to 2,179,859.64 DAI, and the amount Unizen said it reimbursed. Recovery is excluded from the exploit-time number: Unizen reimbursed affected users from its own funds and asked the exploiters onchain to return 80 percent within 48 hours; the anchor transaction’s proceeds were not returned and left 0xb660cae1a59336676ea1887b15eb3c0badb90d78 in August 2024."
  ]
